    "narrative": "For Ghost Ride the WHIP, **James Wood** (78.42) anchors today\u2019s lineup as our premier play, benefiting from a high-leverage matchup against Giolito (5.37 xERA). His leadoff spot and strong xwOBA profile make him the top candidate for a high R/RBI floor, while **Austin Riley** (65.80) and **Josh Naylor** (65.73) provide the requisite power-hitting core against mid-tier arms in Paddack and Gallen. We are leaning heavily into **Corbin Carroll** (63.34) despite the tough draw against Kirby; his 87% stolen base probability against a slow delivery makes him an indispensable asset in our pursuit of the league's scarcest category. **Tyler Soderstrom** (61.50) earns a start largely due to park factors, as we are prioritizing his home environment to offset the moderate SP skill of Rod\u00f3n.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Vinnie Pasquantino** (45.93), who narrowly missed the cut behind **Cole Young** and **Zach McKinstry**. While **Vinnie Pasquantino** remains a high-floor asset, the 15% penalty applied for his platoon disadvantage against Gore pushed his efficiency below our current utilization threshold. Conversely, **Henry Bolte** (58.91) secured a spot over him, as the platoon advantage and park factors provided a superior daily efficiency score. We continue to monitor **Gabriel Moreno** (46.50) and **Zach McKinstry** (46.54), who sit dangerously close to our floor; however, they remain in the lineup today as we hedge against the risk of limited utility options. Managers should note that while our lineup is set, the matchups for **Gabriel Moreno** and **Corbin Carroll** against Kirby remain the primary volatility points due to his 3.46 xERA, making them the most likely candidates to underperform their projections if the early innings go south.",
